e_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUKumgQ","user":{"login":"Skywolf285","id":49045791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MDQ1Nzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49045791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285","html_url":"https://github.com/Skywolf285","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-12T20:11:54Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T20:12:23Z","body":"> > does it fix #117468?\r\n> \r\n> This PR doesn't seem to fix that issue. In fact, the issue seems to get worse in parts of the scene due to the texel shift:\r\n\r\nThis test isn't conclusive as this test project suffers from another issue I described here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117468#issuecomment-5646648863\r\n\r\nTL:DR: Re-import that model with the option to generate UV2 enabled.\r\n\r\nAll this said, this PR fixes some light leaking but still has issues elsewhere:\r\n\r\nLight seams persist seemingly at edges smaller than 90 degrees:\r\n<img width=\"1149\" height=\"575\" alt=\"AI Slop lm fixes\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f3b483c5-f253-439c-bd2f-abc3f6ea7781\" /> \r\n\r\nHowever due this PR AI assisted nature (and the uncertainty of the extend the code changes were done by AI) am I not sure how much this code can be trusted or can be improved upon by the author. So it feels like a bit like a dead end towards properly fixing Godot's lightmaps. But those are just my two cents as someone who isn't a big fan of anything AI.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5648393857/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]